
A Millions Tears: The Unbreakable Bond

In a world where humans and creatures such as elves, werewolves, and mages coexist, there is an invisible threat spying in different cities and kingdoms. In Regni Lumiere, one of the biggest and most important cities, lived Arden, an 18-year-old mage. He is extraordinary in magic and swordship because he grew up with the elvish royal family in a different kingdom while he attended Regni Lumiere school. Arden is always serious and only has three friends.

While he is riding his horse, Ares, from school to Regni Lumiere, he earns a mellifluous voice calling his name. He adventures in the Forest of Death knowing that it is a cursed place where most creatures that went inside did come out or they did but weren’t themselves. The mellifluous voice keeps calling him until he arrives at an empty space with no trees. A woman wearing all white approaches him from the other side, and says: “I’m the gatekeeper between the worlds. The world you know will collapse and darkness will rule… unless the prophecy came true before the collapse. History cannot repeat itself.” The woman vanished in silence while Arden didn't understand how he got there. Ares, his horse, started neighing in fear when dark creatures ran to them with weapons. The horse ran as fast as possible and Arden used magic to defend himself.

He doesn’t say a word of what happened, but he keeps dreaming about it every time he closes his eyes. A few days later, he meets Auryn, an elf princess from another kingdom from overseas, and they fall in love. They started a relationship and got married in secret and in the eye of society they are close friends. They lived in Arden’s safe house where not even his friends knew where it was. They got pregnant. 

The tenebris, dark creatures, find out that their worst nightmare is about to be born, and they go to war. Faced with no other option, he tells his friends about the prophecy, his marriage, and unborn child. Without giving it a second thought, they agree to be there when they need them. As they participate in a secret order that fights the tenebris, the order members agree to fight by their side. Auryn gives birth to twins. A month later, the couple travel to an elf kingdom because the king and queen are members of the secret society and they are very close friends with Arden. Before they go, Auryn and Arden give more than half their powers to the babies who don’t stop crying. The tenebris find out where their secret place is, and they march to kill them all. Arden, Auryn, Arden’s friends and others get ready to face them, but none of them survive. 17 years later, the tenebris keep reaching for the babies, who grew up as princes of Regni Aethea. As the enemy invaded Regni Aethea, the twins sacrificed themselves to save the elf from extinction.  Before they die, they say, “You may forget the past… but the past has no intention of being forgotten. It is not a place to live because it guards a dark secret that could destroy what we know.”  Part of their souls didn’t die, it was dormant. They walk the earth again, but as strangers and enemies. 
